Description: libavfilter/inlineass: take inlineass_lock in config_input + uninit
 Patch 0100 promoted the per-filter libass mutex to a process-wide
 inlineass_lock and claimed to wrap "every libass entry" — but it wrapped
 only the runtime entries (filter_frame, append_data, replay_chunk,
 set_fonts, add_attachment, set_storage_size) and MISSED the lifecycle
 functions config_input (ass_set_frame_size / ass_set_pixel_aspect) and
 uninit (ass_free_track / ass_renderer_done / ass_library_done).
 .
 On jellyfin-ffmpeg 7.x with a graph reconfigure (probe -> live), the main
 thread tears down the stale filter instance via uninit() while the
 subtitle decoder thread is still feeding the live instance via
 replay_chunk -> ass_process_chunk. libass shares process-global state
 (fontconfig, FreeType cache, font provider) that is not reentrant, so the
 unlocked teardown corrupts it, surfacing as
 `libass/ass.c:127: ass_alloc_event: Assertion 'track->n_events <=
 track->max_events' failed` aborting the decoder thread. config_input has
 the same exposure (runs at graph config, concurrent with an
 already-running sub decoder on the separate-input -map_inlineass path).
 .
 Fix: wrap both lifecycle functions' libass calls in inlineass_lock, so
 ALL libass entry points in vf_inlineass.c are serialised.
Author: scaleplex
Last-Update: 2026-05-23
---
--- a/libavfilter/vf_inlineass.c
+++ b/libavfilter/vf_inlineass.c
@@ -138,12 +138,20 @@
 {
     AssContext *ass = ctx->priv;
 
+    /* scaleplex: serialise libass teardown against the decoder thread's
+     * append/replay and another instance's render. libass shares
+     * process-global state (fontconfig/freetype) that is NOT reentrant;
+     * graph reconfig (probe->live) frees a stale instance here while the
+     * sub decoder may still feed the live one. 0100 wrapped the runtime
+     * libass entries but missed init/config_input/uninit. */
+    pthread_mutex_lock(&inlineass_lock);
     if (ass->track)
         ass_free_track(ass->track);
     if (ass->renderer)
         ass_renderer_done(ass->renderer);
     if (ass->library)
         ass_library_done(ass->library);
+    pthread_mutex_unlock(&inlineass_lock);
 }
 
 static int query_formats(AVFilterContext *ctx)
@@ -159,9 +167,11 @@
     ff_draw_init(&context->draw, link->format,
                  context->alpha ? FF_DRAW_PROCESS_ALPHA : 0);
 
+    pthread_mutex_lock(&inlineass_lock);
     ass_set_frame_size(context->renderer, link->w, link->h);
 
     ass_set_pixel_aspect(context->renderer, av_q2d(link->sample_aspect_ratio));
+    pthread_mutex_unlock(&inlineass_lock);
 
     return 0;
 }
